Use Google Cloud Secret Manager for production scripts — especially trigger-based scripts. [NEW]
Script Properties are acceptable only for low-sensitivity scripts with restricted edit access.
Scopes and Permissions
Explicitly declare all scopes in appsscript.json.
Audit and revoke unnecessary scopes regularly using Google's security tools.
Be cautious with triggers and shared scripts — they can be leveraged maliciously if scopes are too broad.
Execution Model and Deployment  [NEW]
Explicitly choose and document your execution identity — 'Execute as Me' is not a safe default.
Use a dedicated service account as the deployer for production scripts, not a personal account.
Set access level to 'Anyone within the Organization' as the default — never 'Anyone (public)' without AppSec approval.
Trigger Security  [NEW]
Document trigger ownership — installable triggers run with the installer's credentials.
Audit triggers quarterly. Remove unused triggers immediately.
Have an emergency disable procedure for every production trigger.
Third-Party Libraries  [NEW]
Verify every library Script ID against official documentation — never trust an AI-provided Script ID alone.
Pin libraries to specific versions. Never auto-update production libraries without review.
Review library code before adding it — treat it like any other third-party dependency.
AI-Assisted Development  [NEW]
Never include internal credentials, endpoints, or PII in AI prompts.
Treat AI-generated code as untrusted — review it the same way you would review code from an unknown external contributor.
You are responsible for the security of code you deploy, regardless of whether AI generated it.
Always audit AI-generated scope lists — they are almost always over-permissioned.
Logging  [NEW]
Never log secrets, tokens, or full API response bodies.
Review every Logger.log() and console.log() in AI-generated code before deployment.
Use Cloud Logging for production scripts — access is controlled separately from script edit access.
Define a log retention policy and a named reviewer for every production script.
Input Validation  [NEW]
Validate all inputs — sheet values, form submissions, API responses — before use.
Never pass raw user input to external APIs without validation and encoding.
Sanitize HTML output in HTMLService to prevent XSS.





